  "worked_solution": "To find the roots of the polynomial, we must solve the equation $p(w)=0,$ that is\n\n$$\n60{w}^{6}-105{w}^{5}+45{w}^{4}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $15{w}^{4}.$ We can factor out the $15{w}^{4}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{w}^{4}(4{w}^{2}-7w+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $4{w}^{2}-7w+3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{w}^{4}(4{w}^{2}-7w+3) & =0 \\\\ 15{w}^{4}(4w-3)(w-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $w=0,$ $w=\\frac{3}{4},$ and $w=1.$",
